  "playtest": "Playtest: saved-capture harness used actual version10 synthetic saved construction on a worker, compared captured package bytes against independent full replay, exported/imported the self-contained package, restored one model into an empty-dependency destination using real StructureEngine/LocalGame authoritative placement and durable save, reopened saved state, and exercised one-operation undo/repeat. A separate test-only version10 serialization of the placed construction then rendered in actual Main --inspect-world on inherited DISPLAY with an isolated profile. Expected and observed red/grey wall, blue model/water, green fractional piece, camera chunk crossing, loading then hit, F10 recording, generic malformed-file status, cancel-before-poll and observer/cleanup failure isolation. Source bytes stayed unchanged, scratch/Mesh resources cleaned and no edit/capture authority opened in the inspector. The separate real GLFW/OpenGL replay suite exercised cache/worker/source, owner/replacement/save, read-only paging, model, lighting/sky/water rendering and GPU lifecycle regressions. Browser testing does not apply to this native desktop integration. The ordinary full Main capture/menu workflow was not rerun this phase; its prior exact-source run and media remain in structure-inspector-client-validation.json at the parent head. This phase does not add a menu entry for saved-file capture.",
